@fn parse
@purpose Top-level entry: consume a token stream and emit a root EkBlock AST pointing into a populated NodePool.
@pre tokens is non-empty; first token is the EOF sentinel (lexer convention). [src: parser.aria:126]
@post Returns ParseResult with a root EkBlock node and a complete NodePool + any diagnostics. [src: parser.aria:188-189]
@thread_safety immutable — Parser and NodePool are value types. [src: parser.aria:16-22]

---

@fn build_decl_index
@purpose Fast decl-index builder. Scans tokens once to record (name, kind, body_start, body_end) for every top-level decl without constructing the full expression AST.
@pre Tokens array complete; pos and len valid. [src: parser.aria:212-213]
@post Returns ParseResult with DeclIndex listing every decl and a populated AST pool. [src: parser.aria:567-570]
@complexity O(n) token scan with O(m) bracket-balanced skipping per body. [src: parser.aria:272-565]
@antipatterns Decl boundaries rely on NEWLINE tokens which the lexer may omit after keyword-named module paths (e.g. `use test`). Compensated by looking at the previous token (`use` or `.`) before consuming. [src: parser.aria:245-269, parser.aria:453-484]

