@fn _parse_expr
@purpose Pratt expression parser: parse an expression whose infix ops have binding power >= min_bp.
@pre p positioned at a valid expression start (atom, prefix op, or keyword like `if`, `match`). [src: parser.aria:1817]
@post Returns PR with the root expression node and the updated parser position. [src: parser.aria:1881]
@complexity O(n) in tokens consumed; recursion depth bounded by operator nesting. [src: parser.aria:1816-1882]
@antipatterns Multi-line pipelines need explicit lookahead across NEWLINEs for `|>` to work — if you add a new infix that spans lines, replicate that logic. [src: parser.aria:1825-1830]

